                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
                  %h2#universal_constructions Universal constructions
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-adjunction
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Kan+extension"} (∞,1)-Kan extension
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} (∞,1)-limit
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
                  %h2#extra_properties_and_structure Extra properties and structure
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+cube"} cosmic cube
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-category
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-category"}> strict ∞-category
                          ,
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} strict ∞-groupoid
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
                  %h2#1categorical_presentations 1-categorical presentations
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category theory
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/higher+category+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#remarks"} Remarks
              %li
                %a{:href => "#in_homotopy_theory"} In homotopy theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#for_categories"}
                  For
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong delooping hypothesis
            is one of the “guiding hypotheses of higher category theory.” Like the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-category
            should satisfy. It states that:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-categories
              can be identified with
              = succeed "-tuply" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k-j)
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (j-1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+connected+n-category"} simply connected
              = succeed "-categories," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+j)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi j
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\le j \le k
          %p
            The identification involves a degree shift: the
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "-tuply" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i+j)
            = succeed "-tuply" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k-j)
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+j)
          %p
            Here
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              \-(simply) connected
            means that any two parallel
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \leq j
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              \-tuply monoidal
            is interpreted as meaning
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            to be of the form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-category"} (n,r)
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,r)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo +
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,r)+j=(n+j,r+j)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo +
                    %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty+j=\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo =
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j=k
            we have:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              \-tuply monoidal
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-connected" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k-1)
              = succeed "-categories." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+k)
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+j)
            = succeed "-tuply" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is called its
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              \-fold delooping
            and sometimes written
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi j
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^j C
            = succeed "-tuply" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *\in C
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega C = C(*,*)
            which is a
            = succeed "-tuply" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k+1)
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
          %h2#remarks Remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Not infrequently the delooping hypothesis is used to supply a
                %em definition
                of “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                \-tuply monoidal
                = succeed "-category.\u201D" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-category
                for an investigation in low dimensions.
            %li
              %p
                The delooping hypothesis is closely related to the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization+hypothesis"} stabilization hypothesis
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+2
                times, it can automatically be delooped infinitely many times.
            %li
              %p
                In low dimensions, the delooping hypothesis is a special case of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/exactness+hypothesis"} exactness hypothesis
          %h2#in_homotopy_theory In homotopy theory
          %p A “groupoidal” version of the delooping hypothesis may be stated as
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+groupal+n-groupoid"} tuply groupal
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-tuply" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k-j)
              = succeed "-connected" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (j-1)
              = succeed "-groupoids," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+j)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi j
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\le j\le k
          %p
            Here “groupal” means “monoidal and such that all objects have inverses.” (This can actually be seen as a special case of the delooping hypothesis for
            = succeed "-tuply" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,r)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            set to
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=\infty
            the groupoidal delooping hypothesis can be interpreted (via the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "-spaces\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            times. In particular, grouplike
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity-space"} spaces
            can be delooped once, and grouplike
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %span.newWikiWord
              spaces
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/E-infinity-space"} ?
            can be delooped infinitely many times (producing a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
          %p
            Non-grouplike
            = succeed "-spaces" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            = succeed "-categories," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,0)
            = succeed "-space" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
